  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 20,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.098,
            0.894,
            0.148
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "During the process of respiration, organic compounds such as glucose are broken "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "down to provide energy in the form of ATP. ATP is used to provide energy for other reactions in the cell.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.15,
            0.893,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Respiration may be aerobic or anaerobic. Aerobic respiration makes more energy "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "available to the organism.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.184,
            0.894,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In human beings, the transport of materials such as oxygen, carbon dioxide, food "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and excretory products is a function of the circulatory system. The circulatory system consists of the heart, blood and blood vessels.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.235,
            0.893,
            0.269
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In highly differentiated plants, transport of water, minerals, food and other materials is a function of the vascular tissue which consists of xylem and phloem.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.27,
            0.892,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In human beings, excretory products in the form of soluble nitrogen compounds are removed by the nephrons in the kidneys.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.305,
            0.894,
            0.356
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Plants use a variety of techniques to get rid of waste material. For example, waste "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "material may be stored in the cell-vacuoles or as gum and resin, removed in the falling leaves, or excreted into the surrounding soil.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.404,
            0.61,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "E X E R C I S E S"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.447,
            0.728,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. The kidneys in human beings are a part of the system for (a) nutrition. (c) excretion. (b) respiration. (d) transportation.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.503,
            0.814,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. The xylem in plants are responsible for (a) transport of water. (c) transport of amino acids. (b) transport of food. (d) transport of oxygen.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.556,
            0.733,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. The autotrophic mode of nutrition requires (a) carbon dioxide and water. (c) sunlight. (b) chlorophyll. (d) all of the above.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.611,
            0.892,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. The breakdown of pyruvate to give carbon dioxide, water and energy takes place in (a) cytoplasm. (c) chloroplast. (b) mitochondria. (d) nucleus.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.664,
            0.824,
            0.682
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. How are fats digested in our bodies? Where does this process take place?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.683,
            0.614,
            0.7
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. What is the role of saliva in the digestion of food?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.701,
            0.892,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. What are the necessary conditions for autotrophic nutrition and what are its byproducts?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.734,
            0.893,
            0.767
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. What are the differences between aerobic and anaerobic respiration? Name some organisms that use the anaerobic mode of respiration.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.767,
            0.751,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. How are the alveoli designed to maximise the exchange of gases?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.785,
            0.876,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. What would be the consequences of a deficiency of haemoglobin in our bodies?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.804,
            0.847,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. Describe double circulation of blood in human beings. Why is it necessary?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.822,
            0.893,
            0.839
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. What are the differences between the transport of materials in xylem and phloem?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.84,
            0.892,
            0.873
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13. Compare the functioning of alveoli in the lungs and nephrons in the kidneys with respect to their structure and functioning.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.916,
            0.21,
            0.929
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Life Processes"
            }
          ]
